# Everything the image must NOT contain.
#
# The patterns are deliberately BROAD. Matching only the default filename left demo.db bakeable into the
# image, and FOURWATER_DB can name the database anything — so a build run in a directory with a live roster
# in it would ship every volunteer's contact details inside the container.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
backups/

# Secrets: session key, OIDC client secret, NextCloud app password, Mattermost webhook.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated locally, never part of a deployment.
demo-pattern.json
config/*.tmp

# Not needed at runtime. The suite is deliberately absent: tests are not a deployment artefact.
#
# The rule for tools/ is mechanical and test/image.test.mjs enforces it: anything reachable from a package.json
# script ships, anything else does not. season-fixture.mjs was added here after that test caught it — it is a
# fixture three tests use to write a pattern file, and it had gone straight into the image unnoticed, which is
# what the testkit line below has always been about.
# measure.mjs was caught by the same test on the commit that added it: a harness that seeds 200 volunteers and
# 5,000 audit rows to print timings has no business in a production image, and it was not going to be noticed by
# anybody reading the Dockerfile.
test/
tools/testkit.mjs
tools/season-fixture.mjs
tools/measure.mjs
# sourcewalk.mjs is the shared file-walk the derived audits build their evidence from, with the floor that
# makes an empty walk a failure rather than a green suite. Nothing at runtime reads it.
tools/sourcewalk.mjs
node_modules/
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
*.md
!README.md
tools/deadassert.mjs
tools/proseproof.mjs
.githooks/
